---
description: |
  Inverts the ClickHouse round-trip transforms that the ocsf class
  tables' catch-all write applies to fields ABSENT from the pre-INSERT
  record, so the verify recompute reproduces the stamp-side hash input.
  Runs on the RECONSTRUCTED read-back (the shape from_clickhouse table
  mode yields, or homelab::record_integrity::ocsf::read's sql-mode
  rebuild — byte-identical, lab-verified 2026-11-05): for a nullable
  column the reconstruction emits a null field and for a
  DEFAULT-bearing non-nullable column its default value whenever the
  archived record lacked the field, and Tenzir's serializer omits null
  object fields and null list elements recursively when writing JSON
  columns and the catch-all (the vendored integrations/clickhouse.md
  reference; the from_clickhouse reference:
  "A non-nullable column receives its default value for an event
  without the field, such as 0, '' or {}, and the event comes back with
  that value" — a documented "difference from the original events").
  The stamp-side hash (attest.tql) covers the PRE-INSERT record, so the
  artifact must leave before verify recomputes.

  WHAT IS STRIPPED, per class, is evidence-anchored to the LANDED lanes
  and the store's hand-DDL (config/10-startup-scripts.xml) — the same
  pairing discipline as a new typed column: a new column or a new lane
  re-audits the arm. Stripping only fires when the read-back value
  equals the artifact signature (null for nullable columns, the DEFAULT
  for non-nullable ones); a lane that WRITES that value pre-INSERT
  would collide and must be excluded from the arm:

  - 6003 API_Activity: severity_id == 0 — the k8s-audit lane never
    writes severity_id (all 4,197,949 landed rows read back 0, the Int8
    DEFAULT 0; live count 2026-11-05).
  - 1007 Process_Activity: process.path == null — the tetragon maps
    write process.file.path and actor.process.path, never process.path
    (475,776 landed rows carry the null artifact); device.hostname ==
    null — `$ocsf.device.hostname = move $input.node_name?` never
    writes a real null (absent node_name = absent field, 0 landed
    nulls), and the emptied device parent drops with it.
  - 1001 File_System_Activity: actor.process.container.name == null —
    the kprobe map builds the container only when the process has a
    pod (3,906 landed rows carry the null artifact; the emptied parent
    drops); device.hostname == null — same move semantics as 1007.
    file.xattributes.permission is NEVER stripped: the kprobe literal
    always writes it, null included, so a null read-back is the REAL
    pre-INSERT value (0 landed nulls).
  - 4001 Network_Activity: traffic.bytes == null — no landed row ever
    wrote it (13,574,131 attested rows: zero event JSON carries a
    traffic object at all; the null artifact is the whole of the
    read-back's traffic, so the emptied parent drops). src/dst
    endpoint IPs are NEVER stripped: both lanes write real values.
  - 0 Base_Event: device.hostname == null — the fleet lane writes it
    from hostIdentifier (always real), the tetragon fallback moves
    node_name (absent-able, never real-null). class_name is NEVER
    stripped: ocsf_derive fills it ("Base Event") before the stamp.
  - 2004 Detection_Finding and 2002 Vulnerability_Finding: nothing —
    findings/stamp writes uid/rule_id/subject_* on every finding (null
    included: rule_id is a REAL null on all 3,978 landed trivy rows,
    and a real null lifts to the column and reads back as the same
    null — parity holds without a strip), severity_id/status_id/
    finding_info.*/metadata.product.name are always lane-written.
  - 3002 Authentication / 3001 Account_Change: nothing today — no row
    has ever landed (authentik lanes, 0 rows live 2026-11-05); when
    they land, their lap re-audits this arm.

  NOT INVERTIBLE HERE: JSON-borne null-valued fields (non-column paths)
  are dropped by Tenzir's serializer on the write path and leave no
  trace in the row — the tetragon maps' unmapped literals (policy_name,
  pod.name, pod.namespace on non-kprobe/non-pod records) are
  irrecoverable, so those chains cannot verify from the row alone (the
  design fork,
  documented in the record_integrity README and pinned by
  tetragon-verify-roundtrip-fork). This operator strips only the
  recoverable column artifacts.
---

// Read-back records only: the walk's read operator calls this per
// class before verify; the package tests drive it with round-trip
// fixtures. Keyed on class_uid (the archive rule routes class_uid to
// the class table 1:1) — ocsf-store read-backs only.
match class_uid? {
  6003 => {
    // API Activity: the Int8 DEFAULT 0 artifact (k8s-audit lane never
    // writes the field).
    if severity_id? == 0 {
      drop severity_id?
    }
  }
  1007 => {
    // Process Activity: the tetragon maps never write process.path
    // (they write process.file.path / actor.process.path), and the
    // nullable hostname column materializes a null for a record whose
    // node_name was absent (move writes nothing, never a real null).
    if process?.path? == null {
      drop process.path?
      if process == {} {
        drop process?
      }
    }
    if device?.hostname? == null {
      drop device.hostname?
      if device == {} {
        drop device?
      }
    }
  }
  1001 => {
    // File System Activity: the kprobe container block is conditional
    // on the pod (absent-able, never real-null); the same hostname
    // move semantics as Process Activity. file.xattributes.permission
    // stays: its literal always writes it, null included.
    if actor?.process?.container?.name? == null {
      drop actor.process.container.name?
      if actor?.process?.container? == {} {
        drop actor.process.container?
      }
    }
    if device?.hostname? == null {
      drop device.hostname?
      if device == {} {
        drop device?
      }
    }
  }
  4001 => {
    // Network Activity: no lane ever wrote traffic.bytes (the null
    // column is pure artifact), and with bytes gone the read-back's
    // traffic is empty — both are injected, both leave.
    if traffic?.bytes? == null {
      drop traffic.bytes?
      if traffic == {} {
        drop traffic?
      }
    }
  }
  0 => {
    // Base Event: hostname via move (fleet's hostIdentifier is always
    // real; the tetragon fallback's node_name is absent-able).
    // class_name is ocsf_derive's, never the artifact.
    if device?.hostname? == null {
      drop device.hostname?
      if device == {} {
        drop device?
      }
    }
  }
  // Detection Finding / Vulnerability Finding / Authentication /
  // Account_Change: every column field is lane-written (values or
  // real nulls) — nothing to strip.
  _ => {}
}
